{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>And the angel of YHWH continued to bar the way.</b> Rashi explained: He showed him the signs of the patriarchs. That is to say: when he came to curse at the outset, the merit of our father Abraham did not stand for them, and Balaam had the way open this way and that, corresponding to Ishmael and the children of Keturah — that is 'and it went into the field.' And again, when he turned and came to curse, the merit of Isaac did not stand for them, and Balaam had the way open from another side, corresponding to Esau son of Isaac — and that is 'and it pressed against the wall.' And when he turned and came to curse, the merit of Jacob stood for Israel, for his progeny was complete, and that is 'where there is no room to turn right or left.'"], :book :numbers, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "פירש״י (Rashi) is rendered as 'Rashi explained'; this is the standard acronym expanded in context."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:19:20.241951777Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}